{
  "dom_id": "step-187825",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence",
  "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $3$ and the common difference is $2.$",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\na_n= a_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}3}$ and the common difference is $d={\\color{red}2}.$ So, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\ta_n\t&= a_{1}+(n-1)d \\[3pt]\n\t\t\t&= {\\color{blue}3} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}2})  \\[3pt]\n\t\t\t&= 3 + 2n -2 \\[3pt]\n\t\t\t& =2n+1\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore the formula for the $n$th term is $a_n = 2n+1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
